A||||10||GT Bastard||slightly rough idle on cold startup...||||5||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||06-11-2000||09:39 PM||||After the car has been sitting overnight it fires right up, but the idle is slightly rough like it wants to die.  Once it has run for a minute or so, it's fine. It's not a big deal, but I'm thinking maybe the cold-start injector?  It'd be easy to swap in a new one, but I thought I might see if anyone had suggestions. <P>thanks! ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phaeton||06-11-2000||11:37 PM||||Or the cold start switch thinks it's warmer than it really is and doesn't leave the cold start injector on long enough.<BR>Or the regular injectors are getting a warmer than real signal until the engine catches up with the sensor.<P>Since everything eventually gets up and runs well, bad initial information is a good suspect.<P>How's the fuel volume at pressure, lots and lots of gas flow during cold starting.  A mechanical gauge reading during crank and start could eliminate some guess work.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ka4nkf||06-11-2000||11:50 PM||||The cold start switch only works while the starter is engaged. Therefore I would think it would be something else like the coolant sensor or the mat sensor.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||06-11-2000||11:51 PM||||GT, my moms car was doing that, and it just kept getting worse and worse until one night I was driving it and the car stalled on the highway.. steering wheel locked (couldn't turn it at all.... it was like it was jammed) and I was in the wrong lane, oncoming traffic.. so I restarted the car and changed lanes quickly.<P>anyway... turns out one of the vacuum lines had come loose.. I'm not quite sure if that's correct, as the local ford dealership tends to not take my parents seriously (cause they're not too car literate...) and often tells them things are fine, without even checking the problem.... it still does the funny idle thing when it starts up, but not as bad now. it goes away after a few seconds.. or as soon as I touch the gas. I'm not sure what's wrong, but it might be a similar problem.||||reg||1
