Z||000010||ka4nkf||12-30-2000||01:10 AM||||Ironhorse. The coolant sensor also tells the ecm the temp of the water and tells the ecm to put more fuel when cold. I will tell you a little trick i did and it works like a charm. I noticed when it was about 40 or 50 degrees the car did not stumble when first started. I put a 10,000 OHM resister across the mat sensor connector, and it makes the computor think it is cold. don't worry about gas mileage, you won't notice any difference.||||reg||1
